hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan in today's  episode I'm going to answer a question  for my forum readers who wrote in about  passion so she wrote in asking I don't  know what my passion is how do I find it  great question and definitely something  that you want to check out before use  launch of business a lot of  entrepreneurs start a company just  trying to make money without doing  something a really passion about and  they rarely end up being successful  you'll find that the ones who are the  most successful are the ones who really  love their business are truly passionate  what they're doing and they're more  likely to be a lot more successful so  it's definitely worth investigating  spending some time doing some  soul-searching to figure out what your  passion is before you go launch your  business because in the long term you  have a much greater chance of success so  in terms of how do you find your  passions a couple ways to do it  the first thing I would look at is what  are you already doing you know outside  of whatever job you have or whatever  you're doing to make money right now  what are you doing that you find really  enjoyable and you're able to help people  add a lot of value to their lives  chances are as well as some things that  you're doing maybe is based around a  hobby that you have or some skill that  you have that you're helping people  maybe it's for free just friends and  family but you find that that they  really appreciate what you're doing and  you're adding a lot of value to a lot  their lives and there is there a way  that you can turn that into a potential  business sometimes you think that we're  good at we're not necessarily super  passionate about so we don't want to  build into anything but often some of  the things we go to and work hard up  just outside on our own if it's a hobby  or a skill there's ways to turn that  into our own business and you'll  probably be excited to go and do that  every morning so it's definitely looking  at what you're doing to help people  because that's what a business is all  about the more you can help people the  more successful you're gonna be the more  money you're gonna make so what are you  doing right now that's already helping  people you're getting really good  feedback even if you're not getting paid  there may be a way to turn it into a  business so that's my first way to look  at it the second way to look at it is  what are some frustrations that you feel  in your own life what are things that  you're struggling with  and you really wish there was a solution  for maybe you can go out and try to find  a solution for it and and help yourself  and also help other people in that  process so is there anything in your own  life your day-to-day existence that you  find really really frustrating you wish  there was a solution out there maybe  there's a way you can create that kind  of solution that would help you and also  help other people who are like you so  quick example for my background when I  sold my first software company I was in  a fortunate position of not having to go  do anything for a while  but I wanted to do something right you  don't want to just sit around and do  nothing all day I'm not the kind of guy  who wants to just sit on the beach all  day long  so the next thing it was hooked up with  a venture capital company and we started  raising expansion capital for companies  and that was something that was  interesting for me and I could also add  a lot of value to my friends because  they were asking how do I raise capital  and how do we go through this process I  want to get my company up and sold and  having gone through the process myself I  then was able to help some of my  entrepreneurial friends who were in my  same city do some of the same things  themselves  so that was where I was able to take  something that it was kind of already  doing on the side and be able to turn  that into more of a business and then  the second thing I did was I launched my  website so I launched seven chemical  calm and at first there wasn't a  business model behind it it was just  something I did because I really liked  doing it I found with my software  business I got started when I was 19 so  pretty young didn't really know anything  about sales or software or running the  business before and I was kind of scared  at the beginning right 19 year old kid  and what I found was you know I was a  little girl wild the next thought I'm  not the first guy to go and try to sell  software and I started researching  companies like Microsoft McAfee Intuit a  couple others and looked at how did they  get started  how did they go from nothing to the  first million and how can I do something  similar and I use those strategies to  help me grow my business and I thought  that could be a really cool way to also  help other entrepreneurs so I launched  comical calm sharing a lot of the famous  entrepreneur profiles and stories that I  found inspired me so the first part of  what I did was a venture capital  business and that was just something I  was doing to help other entrepreneurs  and I found that I was able to you know  make some money in the process as well  by helping them grow their business and  the second part is I launched a  MacArthur comm based on a pain that I  saw for me personally a frustration that  here was this young guy starting the  business had no idea what I was doing  and then realizing that if I just copied  the strategies is why they're famous  entrepreneurs I could achieve some  success on my own as well and out of  that frustration I was able to help  other entrepreneurs and we've built up  now the largest collection of famous  entrepreneur profiles anywhere online so  that was kind of the beginnings of Evan  Carmichael calm and I still love what I  do every day I love helping  entrepreneurs and that's the backbone of  my business I love helping out my  prayers and help them grow their  business and start a new business as  well so that was the discovery I went  through after selling my first offer  company and was able to get to this  point and very grateful for it and  hopefully by going through that same  journey of self-discovery you will find  something you really love and can be  really successful at as well but you  know make sure you don't start anything  until you're you're really passionate  about it don't just do something because  you think you have to do something and  you're just trying to make a buck try to  do something where you feel you're  really excited about it and you think  you can add a ton of value to your  customers and people we're going to  eventually you know pay you for your  services or for your product hope for  the help if you guys liked the video  please give it a thumbs up below I you  know really instead motivates me to want  to make more of these videos for you  guys and if you have a question about  this video or you have a question of  your own about your own company feel  free to leave it in the comments below I  always read those and try to respond to  as many as I can so thank you and we'll  see you on the next episode  you
 

